            <ArticleTitle>The evolving landscape of new diagnostic tests for invasive aspergillosis in hematology patients: strengths and weaknesses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>539-544</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/QCO.0000000000000408</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE OF REVIEW" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The diagnosis of invasive aspergillosis in hematologic patients is a complex composite of clinical preconditions and features, imaging findings, biomarker combinations from appropriate clinical samples and microbiological and/or histological findings.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECENT FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Recent developments in the evolving landscape of diagnostic tests for invasive aspergillosis in adult hematology patients are highlighted.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Novel approaches and tools are currently under development. Focusing optimized diagnostic performance, in particular the combination of biomarkers from appropriate clinical samples, improved diagnostic performance distinctly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
